IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: section 144(e) -- THE DEFINITIONS FOR SECTION 144: control group, controlling
-- stockholder, controlling stockholder transaction, disinterested director and stockholder, going private transaction, material interest,
-- material relationship. Each is "for purposes of this section" (src:419): a predicate worked out from facts. The evaluative standards
-- ("would reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of the director's judgment", "would be material to such stockholder") are
-- inputs the person states, never computed (source-patterns 8.1). "Affiliates and associates" (defined in section 203(c), piece dg3)
-- are taken into the numbers the person states: a person's voting power is stated together with that of its affiliates and associates.
-- The text is de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text).

§ `Section 144(e)(1) and (2): control group and controlling stockholder`

DECLARE `s 144(e)(2) Facts about a person's control` HAS
-- out of range: section 203(c) (piece dg3) defines "affiliates" and "associates"; the person states the voting power already counted together with theirs.
    `the voting power in the election of directors that the person owns or controls, together with its affiliates and associates` IS A NUMBER
    `the voting power in the election of directors of all the outstanding stock entitled to vote generally in the election of directors` IS A NUMBER
    `the person owns or controls a majority in voting power in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has the right, by contract or otherwise, to cause the election of nominees selected at its discretion who constitute a majority of the board of directors or directors entitled to cast a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person owns or controls at least 1/3 in voting power in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has the power to exercise managerial authority over the business and affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVETH A `Vote base`
`s 144(e)(2) the outstanding stock entitled to vote generally in the election of directors as a vote base` MEANS
    `another base named in the provision` "the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote generally in the election of directors"

-- A person is a controlling stockholder if, together with its affiliates and associates, it
--   a. owns or controls a majority in voting power of the outstanding stock entitled to vote generally in the election of directors (or in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors); or
--   b. has the right, by contract or otherwise, to cause the election of nominees selected at its discretion who constitute a majority of the board (or directors entitled to cast a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors); or
--   c. has the power functionally equivalent to that of such a stockholder by virtue of ownership or control of at least 1/3 in voting power (of either base) AND power to exercise managerial authority. Limb c is cumulative.
-- NOTHING when the voting powers stated cannot be a vote (the core's `the vote carries`).
-- src:421 | (2) “Controlling stockholder” means any person that, together with such person’s affiliates and associates:
-- src:422 | a. Owns or controls a majority in voting power of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote generally in the election of directors or in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors on the board of directors;
-- src:423 | b. Has the right, by contract or otherwise, to cause the election of nominees who are selected at the discretion of such person and who constitute either a majority of the members of the board of directors or directors entitled to cast a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors on the board of directors; or
-- src:424 | c. Has the power functionally equivalent to that of a stockholder that owns or controls a majority in voting power of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote generally in the election of directors by virtue of ownership or control of at least ⅓ in voting power of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote generally in the election of directors or in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors on the board of directors and power to exercise managerial authority over the business and affairs of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(e)(2) (src:421-424)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(e)(2) Facts about a person's control`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(e)(2) the person is a controlling stockholder` f MEANS
    `dg2 either finding holds`
        (`dg2 either finding holds`
            (`dg2 either finding holds`
                (`the vote carries` (`a majority of` `s 144(e)(2) the outstanding stock entitled to vote generally in the election of directors as a vote base`)
                    (f's `the voting power in the election of directors that the person owns or controls, together with its affiliates and associates`)
                    (f's `the voting power in the election of directors of all the outstanding stock entitled to vote generally in the election of directors`))
                (JUST (f's `the person owns or controls a majority in voting power in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors`)))
            (JUST (f's `the person has the right, by contract or otherwise, to cause the election of nominees selected at its discretion who constitute a majority of the board of directors or directors entitled to cast a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors`)))
        (`dg2 both findings hold`
            (`dg2 either finding holds`
                (`the vote carries` (`at least` (1 DIVIDED BY 3) `s 144(e)(2) the outstanding stock entitled to vote generally in the election of directors as a vote base`)
                    (f's `the voting power in the election of directors that the person owns or controls, together with its affiliates and associates`)
                    (f's `the voting power in the election of directors of all the outstanding stock entitled to vote generally in the election of directors`))
                (JUST (f's `the person owns or controls at least 1/3 in voting power in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors`)))
            (JUST (f's `the person has the power to exercise managerial authority over the business and affairs of the corporation`)))

DECLARE `s 144(e)(1) Facts about a group of persons` HAS
    `the number of persons in the group` IS A NUMBER
    `none of the persons is a controlling stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the persons are bound together by an agreement, arrangement, or understanding between or among them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by virtue of that agreement, arrangement, or understanding the persons constitute a controlling stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Control group" means 2 or more persons that are not controlling stockholders that, by virtue of an agreement, arrangement, or
-- understanding between or among such persons, constitute a controlling stockholder.
-- src:420 | (1) “Control group” means 2 or more persons that are not controlling stockholders that, by virtue of an agreement, arrangement, or understanding between or among such persons, constitute a controlling stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(e)(1) (src:420)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(e)(1) Facts about a group of persons`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 144(e)(1) the persons are a control group` f MEANS
        f's `the number of persons in the group` AT LEAST 2
    AND f's `none of the persons is a controlling stockholder`
    AND f's `the persons are bound together by an agreement, arrangement, or understanding between or among them`
    AND f's `by virtue of that agreement, arrangement, or understanding the persons constitute a controlling stockholder`

§ `Section 144(e)(3): controlling stockholder transaction`

-- "Controlling stockholder transaction" means an act or transaction between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries, on
-- the 1 hand, and a controlling stockholder or a control group, on the other hand, or an act or transaction from which a controlling
-- stockholder or a control group receives a financial or other benefit not shared with the corporation's stockholders generally.
-- src:425 | (3) “Controlling stockholder transaction” means an act or transaction between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries, on the 1 hand, and a controlling stockholder or a control group, on the other hand, or an act or transaction from which a controlling stockholder or a control group receives a financial or other benefit not shared with the corporation’s stockholders generally.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(e)(3) (src:425)
GIVEN `the act or transaction is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and a controlling stockholder or a control group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a controlling stockholder or a control group receives from the act or transaction a financial or other benefit not shared with the corporation's stockholders generally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 144(e)(3) the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction` `the act or transaction is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and a controlling stockholder or a control group` `a controlling stockholder or a control group receives from the act or transaction a financial or other benefit not shared with the corporation's stockholders generally` MEANS
        `the act or transaction is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and a controlling stockholder or a control group`
    OR  `a controlling stockholder or a control group receives from the act or transaction a financial or other benefit not shared with the corporation's stockholders generally`

§ `Section 144(e)(7) and (8): material interest and material relationship`

DECLARE `s 144(e) Kind of person for a material interest or relationship` IS ONE OF
    `a director, for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)`
    `a stockholder, for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)`
    `a person other than a director or stockholder, for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)`

-- "Material interest" means an actual or potential benefit, including the avoidance of a detriment, other than 1 which would
-- devolve on the corporation or the stockholders generally, that (i) in the case of a director, would reasonably be expected to
-- impair the objectivity of the director's judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization, or approval of the act or
-- transaction at issue and (ii) in the case of a stockholder or any other person (other than a director), would be material to
-- such stockholder or such other person. The two standards are evaluative: the person states them.
-- src:431 | (7) “Material interest” means an actual or potential benefit, including the avoidance of a detriment, other than 1 which would devolve on the corporation or the stockholders generally, that (i) in the case of a director, would reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of the director’s judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization, or approval of the act or transaction at issue and (ii) in the case of a stockholder or any other person (other than a director), would be material to such stockholder or such other person.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(e)(7) (src:431)
GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `s 144(e) Kind of person for a material interest or relationship`
      `there is an actual or potential benefit, including the avoidance of a detriment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit is one that would devolve on the corporation or the stockholders generally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit would reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of the director's judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization, or approval of the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit would be material to the stockholder or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 144(e)(7) the person has a material interest` `the kind of person` `there is an actual or potential benefit, including the avoidance of a detriment` `the benefit is one that would devolve on the corporation or the stockholders generally` `the benefit would reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of the director's judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization, or approval of the act or transaction` `the benefit would be material to the stockholder or other person` MEANS
        `there is an actual or potential benefit, including the avoidance of a detriment`
    AND (NOT `the benefit is one that would devolve on the corporation or the stockholders generally`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the kind of person`
         WHEN `a director, for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)` THEN `the benefit would reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of the director's judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization, or approval of the act or transaction`
         WHEN `a stockholder, for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)` THEN `the benefit would be material to the stockholder or other person`
         WHEN `a person other than a director or stockholder, for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)` THEN `the benefit would be material to the stockholder or other person`)

-- "Material relationship" means a familial, financial, professional, employment, or other relationship that (i) in the case of a
-- director, would reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of the director's judgment when participating in the
-- negotiation, authorization, or approval of the act or transaction at issue and (ii) in the case of a stockholder, would be
-- material to such stockholder. The definition says nothing of a person who is neither: NOTHING.
-- src:432 | (8) “Material relationship” means a familial, financial, professional, employment, or other relationship that (i) in the case of a director, would reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of the director’s judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization, or approval of the act or transaction at issue and (ii) in the case of a stockholder, would be material to such stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(e)(8) (src:432)
GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `s 144(e) Kind of person for a material interest or relationship`
      `the relationship would reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of the director's judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization, or approval of the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship would be material to the stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(e)(8) the person has a material relationship` `the kind of person` `the relationship would reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of the director's judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization, or approval of the act or transaction` `the relationship would be material to the stockholder` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of person`
    WHEN `a director, for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)` THEN JUST `the relationship would reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of the director's judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization, or approval of the act or transaction`
    WHEN `a stockholder, for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)` THEN JUST `the relationship would be material to the stockholder`
    WHEN `a person other than a director or stockholder, for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)` THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 144(e)(4) and (5): disinterested director and disinterested stockholder`

-- "Disinterested director" means a director who is not a party to the act or transaction and does not have a material interest in the
-- act or transaction or a material relationship with a person that has a material interest in the act or transaction.
-- src:426 | (4) “Disinterested director” means a director who is not a party to the act or transaction and does not have a material interest in the act or transaction or a material relationship with a person that has a material interest in the act or transaction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(e)(4) (src:426)
GIVEN `the director is a party to the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has a material interest in the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has a material relationship with a person that has a material interest in the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 144(e)(4) the director is a disinterested director` `the director is a party to the act or transaction` `the director has a material interest in the act or transaction` `the director has a material relationship with a person that has a material interest in the act or transaction` MEANS
        (NOT `the director is a party to the act or transaction`)
    AND (NOT `the director has a material interest in the act or transaction`)
    AND (NOT `the director has a material relationship with a person that has a material interest in the act or transaction`)

-- "Disinterested stockholder" means any stockholder that does not have a material interest in the act or transaction at issue or, if
-- applicable, a material relationship with the controlling stockholder or other member of the control group, or any other person
-- that has a material interest in the act or transaction. The relationship limb applies "if applicable": where the act or transaction
-- involves a controlling stockholder or control group, or another person with a material interest.
-- src:427 | (5) “Disinterested stockholder” means any stockholder that does not have a material interest in the act or transaction at issue or, if applicable, a material relationship with the controlling stockholder or other member of the control group, or any other person that has a material interest in the act or transaction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(e)(5) (src:427)
GIVEN `the stockholder has a material interest in the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship limb applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has a material relationship with the controlling stockholder or other member of the control group, or any other person that has a material interest in the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 144(e)(5) the stockholder is a disinterested stockholder` `the stockholder has a material interest in the act or transaction` `the relationship limb applies` `the stockholder has a material relationship with the controlling stockholder or other member of the control group, or any other person that has a material interest in the act or transaction` MEANS
        (NOT `the stockholder has a material interest in the act or transaction`)
    AND (NOT (`the relationship limb applies` AND `the stockholder has a material relationship with the controlling stockholder or other member of the control group, or any other person that has a material interest in the act or transaction`))

§ `Section 144(e)(6): going private transaction`

DECLARE `s 144(e)(6) Facts about the transaction` HAS
-- out of range: sections 12(g) and 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (federal law, not among the inputs): a plain fact.
    `the corporation has a class of equity securities subject to section 12(g) or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 or listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: 17 CFR 240.13e-3(a)(3) (federal regulation, not among the inputs): whether the transaction is a "Rule 13e-3 transaction" is a plain fact.
    `the transaction is a Rule 13e-3 transaction as defined in 17 CFR 240.13e-3(a)(3) or any successor provision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all or substantially all of the shares held by the disinterested stockholders, but not those of the controlling stockholder or control group, are cancelled, converted, purchased, or otherwise acquired or cease to be outstanding pursuant to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Going private transaction" means: a. for a corporation with a class of equity securities subject to section 12(g) or 15(d) of the
-- Securities Exchange Act of 1934 or listed on a national securities exchange, a "Rule 13e-3 transaction" (as defined in 17 CFR
-- 240.13e-3(a)(3) or any successor provision); and b. for any other corporation, any controlling stockholder transaction, including a
-- merger, recapitalization, share purchase, consolidation, amendment to the certificate of incorporation, tender or exchange offer,
-- conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, pursuant to which all or substantially all of the shares held by the
-- disinterested stockholders (but not those of the controlling stockholder or control group) are cancelled, converted, purchased, or
-- otherwise acquired or cease to be outstanding. Whether a transaction is a Rule 13e-3 transaction is federal law (not among the
-- inputs): a fact the person states.
-- src:428 | (6) “Going private transaction” means:
-- src:429 | a. For a corporation with a class of equity securities subject to § 12(g) or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 [15 U.S.C. § 78l(g) or § 78o(d)] or listed on a national securities exchange, a “Rule 13e-3 transaction” (as defined in 17 CFR § 240.13e-3(a)(3) or any successor provision); and
-- src:430 | b. For any other corporation to which paragraph (e)(6)a. of this section does not apply, any controlling stockholder transaction, including a merger, recapitalization, share purchase, consolidation, amendment to the certificate of incorporation, tender or exchange offer, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, pursuant to which all or substantially all of the shares of the corporation’s capital stock held by the disinterested stockholders (but not those of the controlling stockholder or control group) are cancelled, converted, purchased, or otherwise acquired or cease to be outstanding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 144(e)(6) (src:428-430)
GIVEN f IS A `s 144(e)(6) Facts about the transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 144(e)(6) the transaction is a going private transaction` f MEANS
    IF   f's `the corporation has a class of equity securities subject to section 12(g) or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 or listed on a national securities exchange`
    THEN f's `the transaction is a Rule 13e-3 transaction as defined in 17 CFR 240.13e-3(a)(3) or any successor provision`
    ELSE    f's `the transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction`
        AND f's `all or substantially all of the shares held by the disinterested stockholders, but not those of the controlling stockholder or control group, are cancelled, converted, purchased, or otherwise acquired or cease to be outstanding pursuant to the transaction`
